   293	## The form
   294	
   295	KEEP or CUT on R2; ACCEPT or REJECT on the rest. Notes are optional.
   296	
   297	```text
   298	R1  preamble text: ACCEPT / REJECT
   299	R2  service-key listing (AUTHOR RULING): KEEP / CUT
   300	R3  C3 "fails" reading (OWNER CLARIFY): ACCEPT / REJECT
   301	R4  UTC readings, notes 14-15: ACCEPT / REJECT
   302	R5a release envelope and custody contents: ACCEPT / REJECT
   303	R5b "imports" reading: ACCEPT / REJECT
   304	R6  fingerprint channel rule: ACCEPT / REJECT
   305	R7  P1: ACCEPT / REJECT
   306	R8  P2: ACCEPT / REJECT
   307	R9  P3 [model]: ACCEPT / REJECT
   308	R10 P4: ACCEPT / REJECT
   309	R11 P5: ACCEPT / REJECT
   310	R12 P5c, E-02 gap open: ACCEPT / REJECT
   311	R13 P10: ACCEPT / REJECT
   312	R14 P7 type-separation half: ACCEPT / REJECT
   313	R15 P8 bounded claim: ACCEPT / REJECT
   314	R16 P9 contract inspection: ACCEPT / REJECT
   315	R17 E6a with companions: ACCEPT / REJECT
   316	R18 129 strict rows: ACCEPT / REJECT
   317	R19 M2 and M5: ACCEPT / REJECT
   318	R20 E18 sign-off: ACCEPT / REJECT
   319	R21 E8/E7/E11 sheet, gaps named: ACCEPT / REJECT
   320	R22 E12 page: ACCEPT / REJECT
   321	R23 anchored-signature control: ACCEPT / REJECT
   322	R24 window vectors: ACCEPT / REJECT
   323	R25 root-KSK rollover control: ACCEPT / REJECT
   324	R26 signer branch: ACCEPT / REJECT
   325	```
   326	
   327	ACCEPT records your judgment on the statement printed in that row. Owner decisions retain their provenance. R2
   328	separately records your author ruling. REJECT is recorded with any explanation you provide; the owner identifies the
   329	required correction or returns an explicit choice. Rejection alone does not select alternative semantics.
   330	
