   846	## 9. Owner decisions taken here, for the author's record
   847	
   848	D-1 **Number rule: value-preserving (§1.2).** This changes A1 P8's item "numbers not exactly representable as
   849	IEEE 754 doubles" and prereg §4.3's "must be exactly representable". **A9.8 registers it** (A9.7 rows 22–23), as
   850	Codex review 14 asked. The registered wording also fails to compose with RFC 8785 (§1.2). [OWNER 2026-10-19, G38]
   851	*(Was: "It needs an A9 sentence. … The derivation's profile line, which says the rule is unchanged, must be revised
   852	to match." Both are done.)*
   853	D-2 Unicode 16.0.0 is pinned. Unassigned code points are rejected, and text that is not NFC is rejected rather than
   854	normalized.
   855	D-3 Limits: a payload of at most 2^24 bytes; depth 64 for the payload and 62 for content.
   856	D-4 Widths: a u8 tag length, a u16 canonicalization version equal to 1, and a u32 length (G-01 changed from u64).
   857	D-5 One tag for both signers' frames (A5 §A5.4). Slots are told apart by the fingerprint and the manifest order,
   858	and no slot name is written.
   859	D-6 Fingerprint strings carry scheme prefixes: `spki-sha256` for kms and `gpg-sha256` for gpg.
   860	**Owner decision (2026-10-09): no SHA-1 in V1.** The gpg key is bound by SHA-256 over its OpenPGP v4 public-key
   861	packet body, not by the v4 SHA-1 fingerprint, and this applies to the frame, the manifest and the DNS record. The
   862	KMS key stays SHA-256 of its SPKI. Its OpenPGP creation time is unbound, and that is accepted because the
   863	verifier binds the SPKI for that slot (§3.3).
   864	D-7 `manifest_sha256` is computed over the manifest frame. Spec, vectors and preamble are bound by SHA-256 of their
   865	raw bytes.
   866	D-8 *(revised 2026-10-12, findings 4 and 10)* The anchor preimage `A_sig` holds each slot's full frame and its
   867	exact detached signature, in manifest slot order, with a count byte, under the new tag
   868	`tessera-v1/receipt-anchor-sig`. The 2026-10-09 frame-only layout and its tag are withdrawn, with no fallback
   869	(§5.1). The DNSSEC snapshot has its own tagged envelope.
   870	D-9 A closed schema. `declared_issue_time` has second precision with no leap second. D is at most 241 characters.
   871	`binding_forms` is a sorted array.
   872	D-10 OpenPGP signature type 0x00 only. Since 2026-10-12, the anchor codec enforces this (§5.2, rule O).
   873	D-11 The dispatch boundary in §8.
   874	D-12 The DNS record: one RR, one string, a fixed order, no spaces, and the owner name compared without regard to
   875	case. Since 2026-10-12 every field is mandatory, so every canonical value is 255 bytes.
   876	D-13 Reason codes, and the order in which they are reported (§1.4, §3.1, §5, §7). "Trailing bytes" and
   877	"length-prefix mismatch" are reported as `TRAILING` or `TRUNCATED`, and this now includes a signature's own
   878	extent against its slot length. New in 2026-10-12:
   879	- `SIG_EMPTY`, `SIG_PACKET` and `SIG_FORMAT` (§5.2);
   880	- `LENGTH_CAP` for a signature above its cap;
   881	- the verification-stage codes of §5.3;
   882	- `DNS_WINDOW` (§7) and the C4 code `ISSUANCE_WINDOW` (§7.1);
   883	- `DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH` (§7; Amendment 9 disposition, 2026-10-12).
   884	
   885	D-14 *(2026-10-12)* Signature-slot rules are chosen by `(common.alg, slot)`. Rule O is one legacy-header binary v4
   886	packet of at most 1024 bytes. Rule R is raw FIPS 204/205 bytes of the exact parameter-set length. An unregistered
   887	id gets opaque bytes, 1 to 65536 of them.
   888	D-15 *(2026-10-12, finding 6)* The issue order is: frames, sign, verify, freeze the signature bytes, then stamp
   889	`A_sig` (§5.4).
   890	D-16 *(2026-10-12, finding 9)* The git channel's OTS stamp targets the signed commit's object id, never a tree, a
   891	blob or an unsigned commit (§7.2).
   892	D-17 *(2026-10-12, follow-up owner decision)* The issuance window lives in the key-publication record, in both
   893	channels. A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless not-before ≤ declared time and T ≤ not-after. T is the
   894	registered header-time-derived T, with no margin. Key-format expiries are not relied on (§7.1). *Revised
   895	2026-10-12 (Amendment 9 disposition):* both bounds are mandatory and the window is at most 90 days
   896	(`DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`).
